      "note": [
        "Notes  \r\n  \r\nInterest Rate Fixation Period:  \r\nOutstanding loan amount disaggregated by economic activity and interest rate fixation period can vary significantly between months. This is explained by individual loans in certain cases having substantial impact on the disaggregated statistics for a specific industry if the fixation period changes. Even minor adjustments—such as the new fixation period being a few days longer or shorter than previously—can result in the loan being reclassified into a different maturity interval.  \r\n  \r\nGrowth Rates:  \r\nKRITA publishes annual lending growth rates by economic activity and by company size. The overall growth rate for lending to non-financial corporations can be found in the [Financial Market Statistics](https://www.scb.se/fm5001-EN).  \r\nThe base period for ”Growth rate, index” is September 2018.  \r\n  \r\n  \r\nInterest Rates:  \r\nKRITA publishes interest rates by economic activity and by company size. The overall volume-weighted average interest rate for loans to non-financial corporations can be found in the [Financial Market Statistics](https://www.scb.se/fm5001-EN).  \r\n  \r\nBalance Sheet Items and Reclassifications:  \r\n  \r\nApril 2025  \r\nAn increase of approximately SEK 3 billion in outstanding loan amount across all economic activities and company sizes, due to new loan portfolios. Reclassifications have been made to avoid impacting the growth rates statistics.  \r\n  \r\nDecember 2024  \r\nAn increase of approximately SEK 13 billion in outstanding loan amount across all economic activities and company sizes, due to new loan portfolios. Reclassifications have been made to avoid impacting the growth rates statistics.  \r\n  \r\nJanuary 2024  \r\nAn increase of approximately SEK 8 billion in outstanding loan amount across all economic activities and company sizes, due to new loan portfolios. Reclassifications have been made to avoid impacting the growth rates statistics.  \r\n  \r\nSeptember 2023  \r\nAn increase of approximately SEK 21 billion in outstanding loan amount across all economic activities and company sizes, due to new loan portfolios. Reclassifications have been made to avoid impacting the growth rates statistics.  \r\n  \r\nApril 2025  \r\nAn increase of approximately SEK 3 billion in outstanding loan amount across all economic activities and company sizes, due to new loan portfolios. Reclassifications have been made to avoid impacting the growth rates statistics.  \r\n  \r\nSeptember 2022  \r\nAn increase of approximately SEK 12 billion in outstanding loan amount across all economic activities and company sizes, due to new loan portfolios. Reclassifications have been made to avoid impacting the growth rates statistics.  \r\n  \r\nOctober 2019  \r\nAn increase of approximately SEK 15 billion in outstanding loan amount across all economic activities and company sizes, due to new loan portfolios. Reclassifications have been made to avoid impacting the growth rates statistics.  \r\n  \r\nSeptember 2019  \r\nAn increase of approximately SEK 20 billion in outstanding loan amount across all economic activities and company sizes, due to new loan portfolios. Reclassifications have been made to avoid impacting the growth rates statistics."
      ],
